[White "Intro: Structure 2 — Hanging Pawns on c5 & d5: Tension, Blockade & Targeting"]
[Black ""]
[Result "*"]

{ Structure 2 of 5 — Informational Blueprint.<br><br>In the Tartakower and several Queen's Gambit sidelines, Black exchanges knights and advances ...b6 and ...c5, creating hanging pawns on c5 and d5. Our job is to make those pawns static targets rather than a rolling phalanx. } 1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. Bg5 Be7 5. e3 O-O 6. Nf3 h6 7. Bh4 b6 8. cxd5 Nxd5 9. Bxe7 Qxe7 10. Nxd5 exd5 11. Rc1 Be6 12. Qa4 c5 { 12... c5 puts the hanging pawns on the board. Notice we do NOT rush dxc5 right away — holding the d4-c5 tension denies Black easy piece coordination. } { [%csl Gc5,Gd5] [%cal Gd4c5,Ba4c6] } 13. Qa3 Rc8 14. Be2 { After 14. Be2, every hanging-pawn decision follows two clean rules:<br><br>• Strike dxc5 — when Black loses control of d4 or must recapture with a piece, leaving an isolated d5 pawn and a gorgeous d4 blockade.<br><br>• Meet ...c4 with Bb1 and Qc2 — if Black pushes past, aim a battery straight at h7 and undermine the base with b3 or e4. } { [%csl Yd4,Rh7] [%cal Gd4c5,Ba3c5,Be2d3] } *

[Event "Ch0: Foundations — White 1. d4 Repertoire"]
