[White "Intro: Structure 3 — Isolated Queen's Pawn: Attacking With d4 vs Blockading d5"]
[Black ""]
[Result "*"]

{ Structure 3 of 5 — Informational Blueprint.<br><br>In 1. d4 openings you play both sides of the Isolated Queen's Pawn. Against the Tarrasch we blockade Black's d5 pawn surgically with 6. g3; when Black concedes early ...dxc4 and ...c5, we happily play WITH the active d4 pawn ourselves. } 1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 c5 4. cxd5 exd5 5. Nf3 Nc6 6. g3 Nf6 7. Bg2 Be7 8. O-O O-O 9. Bg5 cxd4 10. Nxd4 { Playing AGAINST Black's IQP on d5 is Karpov territory:<br><br>• Trade minor pieces — fewer attackers mean Black cannot justify the weak d5 pawn.<br><br>• Clamp d4 and c5 — put a piece on d4, aim Bg2 down the long diagonal, and keep e2-e4 in reserve until it wins material or creates a second weakness. } { [%csl Rd5,Bd4,Bc5] [%cal Bg2d5,Bd4c6,Bg5f6] } 10... h6 11. Be3 Re8 12. Rc1 Bf8 { — Karpov's setup: pressure on d5 and c6 with Nc3-a4-c5 in mind. Compare with White's own active d4 IQP in Ch1 Line 5.2. } *

[Event "Ch0: Foundations — White 1. d4 Repertoire"]
