[White "Intro: Structure 4 — Closed d5 Space Center: Prophylaxis & Wing Breaks"]
[Black ""]
[Result "*"]

{ Structure 4 of 5 — Informational Blueprint.<br><br>In both the King's Indian Petrosian and the Modern Benoni, White plants a wedge on d5 to claim lasting queenside and central space. Winning these structures means respecting opponent counterplay before launching our own break. } 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. e4 d6 5. Nf3 O-O 6. Be2 e5 7. d5 { 7. d5 locks the center immediately. Black's king-side break ...f5 is coming, while White's natural terrain is the queenside via c4-c5 and b2-b4. } { [%csl Gd5,Ye5] [%cal Gc4c5,Gb2b4,Rf7f5] } 7... a5 8. Bg5 h6 9. Be3 { Our lively Petrosian 9. Be3! avoids trading dark-squared bishops and asks Black how they justify ...h6.<br><br>• Prophylaxis first — protect e4, guard against ...f5-f4 or ...Ng4 leaps, and only then break open the queenside with c4-c5 or b2-b4. } { [%csl Ye4,Rh6] [%cal Be3d2,Gf2f3,Gc4c5,Rf7f5] } 9... Ng4 10. Bd2 f5 11. h3 Nf6 12. exf5 gxf5 { — Sharp Petrosian battle: Black keeps kingside tension while White targets the exposed light squares. } *

[Event "Ch0: Foundations — White 1. d4 Repertoire"]
[Site "Chessable"]
