[White "Intro: Structure 5 — Big Open Center e4 + d4: Consolidate Before You Push"]
[Black ""]
[Result "*"]

{ Structure 5 of 5 — Informational Blueprint.<br><br>Against the Grunfeld Exchange and the QGA 3. e4, White gets the dream pawn duo on d4 and e4. The number-one mistake at club level is pushing d4-d5 too early and handing Black's g7 bishop an open highway. } 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 d5 4. cxd5 Nxd5 5. e4 Nxc3 6. bxc3 Bg7 7. Nf3 c5 8. Bb5+ { With 8. Bb5+ we disrupt Black's pieces first, keeping our d4-e4 center intact.<br><br>• Consolidate before pushing — castle, put rooks on b1 or c1, protect d4 with Be3, and push d4-d5 only when it wins space without hanging c3 or the long diagonal. } { [%csl Gd4,Ge4,Yc3] [%cal Bb5c6,Bc1e3,Ra1b1,Rg7c3] } 8... Nc6 9. Rb1 O-O 10. d5 Ne5 11. O-O { — When Black invites d5 with 8... Nc6, White closes the g7 diagonal with tempo and castles smoothly. Next up: three unannotated GM Model Games showing these blueprints in action. } *

